<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peruvian War of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1809">1809</a>–<a href="/years/1826">1826</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-wars-of-independence">Spanish American wars of independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peruvian War of Independence ended Spanish rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, the stronghold of royalist power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a>'s expedition landed in 1820 and proclaimed independence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in July 1821, but royalist armies held the highlands. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-jose-de-sucre">Antonio José de Sucre</a> won the decisive battles of Junín and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayacucho">Ayacucho</a> in 1824, and the last royalists at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/callao">Callao</a> surrendered in 1826.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peruvian-war-of-independence.jpg" alt="Peruvian War of Independence" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LLs · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peruvian_War_of_Independence_1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
